      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to sum the total number of rounds played by all the golfers and then divide by the total number of golfers.\n\nFrom the chart, we can see the number of rounds played by each golfer:\n- 1 round: 5 golfers\n- 2 rounds: 2 golfers\n- 3 rounds: 2 golfers\n- 4 rounds: 3 golfers\n- 5 rounds: 5 golfers\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total number of rounds played by all golfers:\n\\[ 5 \\text{ rounds} \\times 5 \\text{ golfers} = 25 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\\[ 2 \\text{ rounds} \\times 2 \\text{ golfers} = 4 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\\[ 3 \\text{ rounds} \\times 2 \\text{ golfers} = 6 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\\[ 4 \\text{ rounds} \\times 3 \\text{ golfers} = 12 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\\[ 5 \\text{ rounds} \\times 5 \\text{ golfers} = 25 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\nAdding these together gives the total number of rounds:\n\\[ 25 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 = 72 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of golfers:\n\\[ 5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 17 \\text{ golfers} \\]\n\nThe average number of rounds played by each golfer is the total number of rounds divided by the total number of golfers:\n\\[ \\frac{72 \\text{ rounds}}{17 \\text{ golfers}} \\approx 4.235 \\]\n\nRounded to the nearest whole number, the average number of rounds played by each golfer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{4} \\]",
