      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Sum the total number of rounds played by all golfers.**\n2. **Count the total number of golfers.**\n3. **Divide the total number of rounds by the total number of golfers to get the average.**\n\nLet's start by interpreting the data from the chart:\n\n- **Golfer 1** played 5 rounds.\n- **Golfer 2** played 2 rounds.\n- **Golfer 3** played 2 rounds.\n- **Golfer 4** played 3 rounds.\n- **Golfer 5** played 5 rounds.\n- **Golfer 6** played 4 rounds.\n- **Golfer 7** played 3 rounds.\n- **Golfer 8** played 5 rounds.\n- **Golfer 9** played 5 rounds.\n- **Golfer 10** played 5 rounds.\n- **Golfer 11** played 4 rounds.\n- **Golfer 12** played 3 rounds.\n- **Golfer 13** played 5 rounds.\n- **Golfer 14** played 6 rounds.\n- **Golfer 15** played 6 rounds.\n- **Golfer 16** played 4 rounds.\n- **Golfer 17** played 4 rounds.\n- **Golfer 18** played 3 rounds.\n- **Golfer 19** played 5 rounds.\n\nNow, let's sum the total number of rounds:\n\n\\[\n5 \\text{ (Golfer 1)} + 2 \\text{ (Golfer 2)} + 2 \\text{ (Golfer 3)} + 3 \\text{ (Golfer 4)} + 5 \\text{ (Golfer 5)} + 4 \\text{ (Golfer 6)} + 3 \\text{ (Golfer 7)} + 5 \\text{ (Golfer 8)} + 5 \\text{ (Golfer 9)} + 5 \\text{ (Golfer 10)} + 4 \\text{ (Golfer 11)} + 3 \\text{ (Golfer 12)} + 5 \\text{ (Golfer 13)} + 6 \\text{ (Golfer 14)} + 6 \\text{ (Golfer 15)} + 4 \\text{ (Golfer 16)} + 4 \\text{ (Golfer 17)} + 3 \\text{ (Golfer 18)} + 5 \\text{ (Golfer 19)}\n\\]\n\nSumming these values:\n\n\\[\n5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 + 4 + 3 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 4 + 3 + 5 + 6 + 6 + 4 + 4 + 3 + 5 = 85\n\\]\n\nNext, we count the total number of golfers:\n\n\\[\n19 \\text{ golfers}\n\\]\n\nNow, we compute the average number of rounds played per golfer:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average} = \\frac{\\text{Total rounds}}{\\text{Total golfers}} = \\frac{85}{19}\n\\]\n\nPerforming the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{85}{19} \\approx 4.4737\n\\]\n\nRounding to the nearest whole number: